WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:04.590
The overview is the most important paragraph in Task 1,

00:04.940 --> 00:08.740
and it's the one that most people forget to do.

00:09.660 --> 00:11.530
If you don't write an overview,

00:11.550 --> 00:16.020
you won't get more than a Band 5 for Task Achievement,

00:16.040 --> 00:18.550
so it can drastically affect your score.

00:18.950 --> 00:20.980
Let's have a look for an overview together.

00:21.670 --> 00:22.880
Here's a café.

00:23.070 --> 00:26.270
The graph shows how many cups of coffee it sold

00:26.290 --> 00:29.600
each hour, from 7am to 1pm.

00:29.970 --> 00:31.880
Compare the start and the end.

00:31.900 --> 00:34.300
I'm going to cover the middle.

00:34.460 --> 00:39.210
At 7am, the café sold 20 cups of coffee.

00:39.890 --> 00:42.050
At 1pm, 40 cups.

00:42.180 --> 00:43.860
So sales doubled.

00:44.290 --> 00:46.990
The next step is to find the highest and lowest points.

00:47.010 --> 00:51.880
So sales peaked at 60 cups between 8 and 9am,

00:51.900 --> 00:55.590
and the lowest point was at 7am, surprisingly,

00:55.610 --> 00:59.150
given that most people need coffee at that time,

00:59.170 --> 00:59.930
but still.

00:59.950 --> 01:03.870
Step three would be to describe the shape

01:03.890 --> 01:06.530
in between. Sales rose sharply,

01:06.550 --> 01:08.970
they stayed stable for an hour,

01:09.160 --> 01:12.940
then fell and fluctuated until 1pm.

01:13.320 --> 01:15.210
Now I can write my overview.

01:15.250 --> 01:18.930
Overall, coffee sales doubled over the morning,

01:18.950 --> 01:23.000
with the busiest period between 8am and 9am.

01:23.280 --> 01:26.940
Notice something about this sentence that maybe looks different

01:26.960 --> 01:30.480
to what the rest of Task 1 would look like.

01:30.870 --> 01:31.900
What do you think?

01:32.890 --> 01:34.930
There are no numbers in it.

01:34.950 --> 01:37.840
The overview gives you the big picture.

01:38.100 --> 01:42.470
The detailed figures come in later, in your body paragraphs.

01:42.490 --> 01:47.740
So that's where you put all your numbers and figures: in the body paragraphs.

01:48.120 --> 01:51.610
When I was an examiner, I looked for the overview first.

01:51.640 --> 01:55.440
If there wasn't a clear one, the score for Task Achievement was limited,

01:55.570 --> 01:57.310
however accurate the rest was.

01:57.330 --> 02:00.770
So start it with “Overall” and then a comma,

02:00.950 --> 02:02.830
and make it easy to find.

02:02.850 --> 02:06.500
Normally, I tell students to do it after the introduction.

02:06.580 --> 02:10.420
If you want, you can put it at the end of the essay as well,

02:10.440 --> 02:13.940
as a kind of summary or conclusion.

02:13.960 --> 02:16.640
But I do think sometimes it's better to just put it after

02:16.660 --> 02:19.640
the introduction, so you don't forget to do it,

02:19.660 --> 02:22.050
because you are under pressure when you're in the exam.

02:22.380 --> 02:24.860
On the right page now, there's a new graph:

02:24.880 --> 02:28.070
visitors to a city museum across one year.

02:28.440 --> 02:33.260
First, label each section of the line, and then choose the best overview.

02:33.490 --> 02:37.110
Use the same three steps: start and end,

02:37.310 --> 02:40.410
highest and lowest, and then the shape.
